      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(update-check): wrap malformed npm view JSON parse in try/catch",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`fetchNpmPackageTargetStatus` already bounds the `npm view --json` stdout to 1 MiB, but the bounded string is passed to a bare `JSON.parse`. If npm ever returns malformed JSON with exit code 0, the parse throws a raw `SyntaxError` and crashes the caller.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrapped `JSON.parse` inside `parseNpmPackageTargetMetadata` with a contextual `try/catch`. The error is rethrown with the parse cause and is then caught by the existing `fetchNpmPackageTargetStatus` catch block, so the function returns `{ version: null, nodeEngine: null, error: ... }` instead of crashing.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUpdate/status checks become resilient to malformed npm metadata responses; gateways no longer crash on a transient npm-side JSON glitch.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTerminal proof (after fix):\n\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/update-check-malformed-npm-json.mts\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n=== Proof: update-check malformed npm view JSON ===\n\nSimulating npm view with exit code 0 and invalid JSON stdout...\n\nResult: {\n  \"target\": \"openclaw\",\n  \"version\": null,\n  \"nodeEngine\": null,\n  \"error\": \"Error: npm view returned invalid JSON: SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'o', \\\"not valid json {\\\" is not valid JSON\"\n}\n\nPASS: malformed npm view JSON is caught and surfaced as an error.\n```\n\nRegression test:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/update-check.test.ts\n```\n\nAll 32 tests pass.\n",
        "branch": "fix/update-check-malformed-npm-json",
